 {
  "id": "096",
  "name": "Noel",
  "subtitle": "every Noel's planet",
  "story": "On Noel, Christmas lights don't twinkle; they turn night into day. A string round the porch gets you a decent dawn. A whole street gets you mid-morning. Dad did the whole hill. Clive next door had a look at it over the fence, went to the shops and came back with noon. Nobody on the street has had a night since the first of December. They nod off in armchairs on the pavement, in broad daylight, in their coats. Dad's bought a bigger ladder.",
