   "end": "She's a teenager. Reappears for lifts.",
   "caption": "Keep an eye on Dad.\n\nPeep: 1.1 million people, a 22-hour day, one moon, and peekaboo that really works. Cover your eyes and you're gone; uncover them and you're back, usually where you left yourself. Babies here run the house. Parents spend whole afternoons blinking in and out of the garden, and grandparents are advised to sit down first.\n\nI played it once with a baby on a train. I came back two stops later.\n\n(Child psychologists reckon babies only work out that things still exist when they can't see them at somewhere around eight months. It's called object permanence. On Peep, it's optional.)\n\nHow long could you keep it up?"
  },
